Package: tidysynthesis
Title: Tidy Meta-Analysis and Evidence Synthesis
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Jimmy", "Moses", , "jimmy.moses@pnguot.ac.pg", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3342-2384"))
Description: A tidy toolkit for meta-analysis and evidence synthesis.
    Computes standardised mean differences (Hedges' g), mean differences,
    log risk, odds and incidence rate ratios, Fisher's z and logit
    proportions; pools them with common-effect and random-effects models
    using restricted maximum likelihood, DerSimonian-Laird, Paule-Mandel
    and Sidik-Jonkman estimators with Hartung-Knapp-Sidik-Jonkman
    adjustments and prediction intervals; fits meta-regression, subgroup,
    three-level and phylogenetic models; performs frequentist
    contrast-based network meta-analysis with P-scores and inconsistency
    diagnostics; and provides publication bias diagnostics (Egger, Begg,
    trim-and-fill, PET-PEESE, fail-safe N) and sensitivity analyses. All
    estimators are written in base R. The package integrates with
    'tidymodels' through 'recipes' steps, 'rsample' resampling schemes,
    'yardstick' metrics and a 'parsnip' model specification, and returns
    'tibble' subclasses with 'broom' style tidiers and 'ggplot2' plots.
    Methods follow DerSimonian and Laird (1986) <doi:10.1016/0197-2456(86)90046-2>,
    Viechtbauer (2005) <doi:10.3102/10769986030003261>,
    Rucker and Schwarzer (2015) <doi:10.1186/s12874-015-0060-8> and
    Duval and Tweedie (2000) <doi:10.1111/j.0006-341x.2000.00455.x>.
